ot) Getting By in America is a book written by Barbara Ehrenreich. Written from her perspective as an undercover journalist, it sets out to investigate the impact of the 1996 welfare reform act on the working poor in the United States. The events related in the book took place between spring 1998 and summer 2000. The book was first published in 2001 by Metropolitan Books. It was expanded from an article she wrote from a January 1999 issue of Harper's Magazine. Ehrenreich later wrote a companion book, Bait and Switch (published September 2005), about her attempt to find a white-collar job. In 2019, the book was ranked 13th on The Guardian's list of the 100 best books of the 21st century. In 2024, it was ranked 57th on The New York Times's list of the 100 best books of the 21st century.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nickel_and_Dimed","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"Nickel and Dimed","author":"Barbara Ehrenreich","publisher":"Metropolitan Books","publicationDate":"2001","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"224 pp","isbn":"0-8050-8838-5","language":"English","genre":"Undercover journalism"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-nickel-and-dimed-on-not-getting-by-in-america-barbara-ehrenreich"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-latimes-current-interest-wikipedia-los-angeles-times-book-prize-for-current-interest","label":"Wikipedia: Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Current Interest","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times_Book_Prize_for_Current_Interest","accessedAt":"2026-08-20T21:35:58.016Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/books"},{"id":"source-open-library-nickel-and-dimed-on-not-getting-by-in-america-barbara-ehrenreich","label":"Open Library summary metadata for Nickel and Dimed: On (